Confirmed, no external DNS on that box and no proxy set. Two ways forward.

**Set the proxy and clone directly**

```bash
export https_proxy=http://y84451117:PASSWORD@Hkgpqwg00206.huawei.com:8080
export http_proxy=$https_proxy
curl -I https://gitcode.com --max-time 10
```

Substitute your real password. If curl returns headers, clone normally. If it fails the same way, that proxy isn't reachable from this machine either.

**Clone on fremont and copy over**

This is the surer route, since fremont demonstrably clones from gitcode. From a fremont shell:

```bash
cd ~
git clone https://gitcode.com/TritonAscendTest/Q3TritonKernel.git
scp -r Q3TritonKernel root@141.61.33.141:/home/yaolu/
```

Then back on the A5:

```bash
cd /home/yaolu/Q3TritonKernel
ls
```

For scp to work, fremont needs to authenticate to the A5. It could already reach it on port 22, which is why ProxyJump worked, but it may prompt for the root password.

Worth a quick word to Hocky either way. He expects you to clone repos on that machine, so there's presumably a normal way people do it, whether that's an internal mirror or a proxy setting you don't have yet. Asking takes a minute and saves guessing.
